data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

**Sync I/O on the Cosmos DB provider is fully removed.** In .NET 10, you had an opt-in to allow sync-over-async. In EF Core 11, that opt-in no longer exists — calling any synchronous API **always throws** at runtime.

All four of your methods are affected:

```csharp
// All of these will throw in EF Core 11:
_context.Products.ToList();
_context.Products.First(p => p.Id == id);
_context.Products.Count();
_context.SaveChanges();
```

**Fix — convert to async:**

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

There is no workaround or opt-in — async is now mandatory for the Cosmos DB provider. You'll need to propagate `async/await` up through callers as well.
